    "title": "Chipotle Offers BOGO Deal for Tattooed Customers on Friday the 13th",
    "text": "Do you like Chipotle? Great, we love it too! Do you have tattoos? Very cool, quite a few of us at Nerdist have some permanent ink, just like you. If you have both of them, then you’re in luck for Friday the 13th. If you can escape the clutches of Jason Voorhees, then head over to Chipotle, show them your tattoo, and take advantage of a BOGO special in the restaurant. That’s right, Chipotle is offering a BOGO food special for anyone who bears tattoos because, well, the company’s bag is kinda tatted up. Chipotle/PR NewswireAccording to Chipotle’s websiteOpens in a new tab, customers can come in between 3PM and 4PM on March 13 for a flash BOGO sale if they are “tatted like a Chipotle bag.” This promotion is inspired by the Friday the 13th “flash tattoo” tradition, when tattoo shops drop “flash sheets” of small, pre-designed tattoos. Now, if you don’t have a tattoo or you aren’t rocking a full sleeve of artwork, that’s okay. You can have permanent ink, a temporary tattoo, or hand drawn art to qualify. The Chipotle tattoo BOGO deal is limited to five free items per check and the free item must be of equal or lesser value than the purchased one. And no, kids’ meals do not count as an entree. For more details about this promotion, head over to read Chipotle’s rules and get ready to grab some free food on Friday the 13th.",
